60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B, the Central Study Commons, aligns with the high post-occupancy ratings for bookable spaces.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option B also avoids the off-site space costs. The hall is already there, so no rooms are lost.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A would help the technicians by automating extraction, but it is a high-cost mechanical job.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Option C is out. The weather data makes it too risky. Option B is indoor and safe.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option D has the AV kit issue. No renewal reserve means we will be broke in five years.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, I agree. Option D is a financial trap. Option B is a conversion, not a new build.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@George, Option B requires minimal maintenance. It is just a service desk and some outlets.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,Option B is manageable. The technicians won't be burdened with complex machinery.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Option B is the only one that fits the schedule. No weather, no complex mechanicals.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B is the most cost-effective. The hall is underused, so the capital cost is lower.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I am voting for Option B. It satisfies the post-occupancy criteria and is financially sound.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I am voting for Option B. It solves the timetable disruption issue.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I am voting for Option B. It is a reasonable load for the staff.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I am voting for Option B. It is the only option that respects the calendar.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I am voting for Option B. It avoids the cost inflation and lifecycle traps of the others.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
